hypotheses.statement:
There is an absolute positive integer $B_*$ such that, for all sufficiently large integers $t$, every graph $P$ with $h(P)<t$ and disjoint vertex sets $A,T$ satisfies $$\label{density:incidence-bound}
 \sum_{\substack{v\in T\\ |N_P(v)\cap A|\ge B_*t}}
       |N_P(v)\cap A|
 \le t^{1+2\epsilon}|A|.$$ In particular, $$\bigl|\{v\in T:|N_P(v)\cap A|\ge B_*t\}\bigr|
 \le t^{2\epsilon}|A|.$$

